{"id": "EUVD-2026-81602", "enisaUuid": "8c7d2249-f694-3485-b5c8-65d902485f06", "description": "vm2 versions from 3.11.0 before 3.11.8 fail to protect host TypedArray and ArrayBuffer prototypes from sandbox mutation. Attackers can use prototype-walking primitives to reach and modify host Uint8Array.prototype, %TypedArray%.prototype, and ArrayBuffer.prototype, causing host-created typed arrays to observe attacker-controlled properties after VM.run() returns.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T13:46:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-18T19:49:31", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:H/SA:H", "references": ["https://github.com/patriksimek/vm2/security/advisories/GHSA-3vgf-8m4q-q4qr", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vm2-3.11.0-through-3.11.7-prototype-pollution-via-typedarray"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5v7w-95g5-pj6q", "GHSA-3vgf-8m4q-q4qr", "CVE-2026-92953"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.5, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b6c3ab5c-2dba-378b-a318-2897f52b9721", "product": {"name": "vm2", "vendor": {"name": "patriksimek"}}, "product_version": "3.11.0 <3.11.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a764407a-6635-3fc0-893e-306bb216b88f", "vendor": {"name": "patriksimek"}}], "isExploited": false}